codex
Implemented the Track B generator based on the paper’s Section 4 permutation-graph reduction. The construction uses a unique four-cycle XOR invariant, with a 281-operation compact route versus roughly 27,791 bit operations for exact GF(2) elimination. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2202.13955v1#S4)

Artifacts:

- [gen_2202_13955.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2202.13955/gen_2202_13955.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2202.13955/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2202.13955/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2202.13955/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2202.13955/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2202.13955/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass, including 0/200,000 random guesses, four adversaries at 0/8, exact uniqueness, scaling, canonicalization, and output/effort caps.

The sole blocker is external hardening: all twelve OpenRouter calls returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” They are correctly recorded as errors—not model failures—so the module is not yet submission-ready. Once quota is restored, the three harness runs must be repeated and their valid results incorporated into the report.
