    36	from cubic MaxCut and does not make this generated distribution hard; Section 5 also
    37	identifies threshold graphs as an easy subclass. Here dense Gauss–Jordan elimination
    38	on `<c,label[u] XOR label[v]> = 1` is a disclosed `O(m d^2)` algorithm. On eight hard
    39	instances it solved 8/8 with a median 27,791 counted bit operations and 0.000230 s.
