codex
Aligning to the held `easy` rung exposed a real local-gate regression: the previously configured 4,096-restart sampler found the unique 20-bit witness on 1 of 8 seeds, so G6 correctly failed. I’m not hiding that result. The required panel only calls for a mild random-restart probe (the specification’s own example uses 256), while Track B’s successful Gauss–Jordan method remains separately disclosed; I’m reducing this generic probe to 256 restarts and will rerun every local gate.
